WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:02.601
-I'm hanging out
with Pete Davidson,

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.937
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.338
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:08.875
-We're about to play a game
we call "Wheel of Opinions."

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.376
Here we go.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:14.714
-♪ Wheel of Opinions ♪

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.716
-Okay, I will hit this button,

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:19.886
which activates
the Opinion Topic Generator.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.387
It'll land on a random topic.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.723
Whatever it is, you have to give
your opinion on it.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.891
Ready for this?
-Okay.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:25.892
-Here we go.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.559
First topic is...

00:00:27.559 --> 00:00:29.629
[ Game show music plays ]

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.400
Okay.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.436
Would you rather be caught
saying, "I went glamping"

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:39.405
or, "I'm hangry"?

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:42.242
-What's glamping?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.243
-Glamping is -- is -- is --

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.378
People say glamping.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.546
It's like glamorous camping,
maybe?

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:49.415
People go like,
"I went glamping."

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:50.583
Yeah, people know it.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:51.917
-People say that?
-Oh, for God's sakes.

00:00:51.917 --> 00:00:53.752
Everybody knows glamping!

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:55.755
Everybody knows
what glamping is!

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.256
-That is Jon Stewart
right there!

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.758
-Glamping is very popular.

00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:02.261
-I'll move over.
-That's Jon Stewart right there!

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.597
Jon!
-Hey, Jon.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.099
-Welcome, Jon, to our --
-Hold on.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.601
Let me put my glasses on

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.603
so I look like my opinions
are smarter.

00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:13.940
-Jon. Thank you, Jon.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.109
You were just streaming the show
from home?

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.611
-I'm at work.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.112
-Yes, I'm sorry.
-I'm still at work.

00:01:20.112 --> 00:01:24.617
You know, Peter, somebody has to
make a living in this household.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.785
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:28.053
And it's me!
-Jon...

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:29.722
He comes home,
he eats the peanut butter,

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.724
he drinks the milk --
he doesn't pay!

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.392
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:38.397
-Jon, do you have an opinion
on glamping or hangry?

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:41.166
-Either one of those should --
and again,

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:43.836
I'm not a man that's speaking
for vigilante justice,

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:47.507
but if you were to use any,
I believe it's not improper

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:52.845
to tie you to the back of
a vehicle, maybe a Citi Bike --

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:56.182
-A Citi Bike! [ Laughs ]
-...and drag you through

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.551
perhaps Sixth Avenue.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.553
-Some people call it
the Avenue of Americas.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.555
-Of course they do.
It's very popular.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.558
-And to have townspeople
curse your name

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.727
and spit upon you.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.395
-Alright, that's a good opinion.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.064
Jon, while you're here, can we
just maybe get your opinion

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:13.399
on a couple other topics?

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.833
Let's try one.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.502
-Jimmy, I was hoping you'd ask.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:19.338
Here's one opinion
you may not know.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.340
I love Pete Davidson.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.175
-Ohh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:25.678
-I love Jon.
-That's a fact.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.179
-He is such a good guy.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.681
-Oh, I love that.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.416
Alright, how about
any opinion on --

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.917
let's see if Pete Davidson
comes up

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:34.921
on the Opinion Topic
Generator.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.155
What?

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.657
Swimming with dolphins.
-How nice!

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.759
-Yeah, I have an opinion
on that.

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:43.596
Your generator
is full of [bleep]!

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.598
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:46.932
-What?!

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.235
What about my generator?

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:52.739
-Your -- Your --
Your topic generator!

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.239
-Yeah, why?

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.576
Swimming with dolphins --
do you have an opinion on it?

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.078
Not the generator.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.246
-Oh, I don't have an opinion
with swimming with them,

00:03:01.246 --> 00:03:03.249
but I am pro-blowhole.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.419
That's all I'll say.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.756
-[ Laughing ] What's wrong --
What is wrong with you, man?

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.091
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.594
Uh, Pete, any...?

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.430
-I think it's a lovely thing to
do with your family on vacation.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.597
-Okay, yeah. Okay.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.265
You think it's --
That's perfect.

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:22.101
Also pro-blowhole.
-Sure.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.936
This is coming from a guy
who's hangry.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:26.271
-Yeah, okay.

00:03:26.271 --> 00:03:28.608
Our final topic.
Here we go.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.577
The Opinion Topic Generator,
Jon.

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.912
-Alright, what do you got?

00:03:33.912 --> 00:03:35.080
-Oh.
[ Audience "ohh"s ]

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.749
-Mets versus Yankees.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.584
I have a feeling where
you're gonna land, Jon.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.553
Pete, do you have an opinion,
Mets versus Yankees?

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:44.557
-I also root for the Mets
because their fans are sad.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.225
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.395
-But as a -- when you're a
New Yorker, you get the choice,

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.231
and why -- you pick the Yankees
'cause they win.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.565
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.234
-You know, first of all...

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.737
-But I always root for --
-You don't get a choice.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.238
-I always root for the Mets.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.074
It's like, it would be nice
for the Mets or Jets

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.075
to win something.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:04.911
Jon? Jonathan?

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:08.748
-As a Mets fan
since the 1960s...

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.918
-Wow.
-I accept Peter's charity.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.119
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:18.123
And as fans, we win nothing,
but it is not a choice.

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.126
My father was born in Brooklyn,

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:22.295
and we were not allowed
to like the Yankees.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:27.299
It was -- He would rather
you smoke cigarettes

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:29.635
in the street

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:34.473
while drinking whiskey naked --
-Yeah, as a child.

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:36.142
-...as a 7-year-old --
by the way,

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:39.145
not a good father --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.280
-He would rather that.
-...than like the Yankees.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.416
-That's correct.
You are a diehard all the way.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.417
Mets all the way, Jon Stewart.

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:47.553
-I believe that --
-[ Bell dings ]

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.388
-...the key phrase there
is "die."

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:50.556
We suck.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:53.225
-Pete Davidson, Jon Stewart,
everybody!

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:54.460
-Thanks, Jon.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.930
-You can see Pete, Jon,
and other great comedians

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.600
this Sunday at "NYC Still Rising
After 20 Years:

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.702
A Comedy Celebration."

